.TH PACKSLIP 1 "October 2026" "packslip" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
packslip \- install and verify authenticated upstream releases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B packslip install
.I PROJECT
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B packslip verify
.I BUNDLE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Packslip installs a complete authenticated upstream release tree and exports
only the commands declared by its signed metadata. It does not run downloaded
code, install dependencies, edit shell setup, or activate environments.
This distribution build includes installation and verification commands.
Run a command with
.B --help
for its complete option reference.
.SH INSTALLATION
.B packslip install owner/repo
uses GitHub discovery. A host-named project uses its signed release list.
.B --version
selects a version, prefix, or tag.
.B --system
selects shared installation; Unix root uses it by default.
.B --user
selects the current user and requires non-root execution on Unix.
.B --install-dir
and
.B --bin-dir
override destinations without moving trust state.
.SH TRUST AND RECOVERY
.B --pin
requires a separately obtained repository fingerprint.
.B --pubkey
requires a public key for key-signed releases.
Administrator pins, caller constraints, and remembered continuity all apply.
.B --force
replaces conflicting command entries and unmarked directories. It never
bypasses trust, freshness, protected paths, or archive safety.
Packslip stages changes and recovers interrupted replacements before the next
install. Once committed, cleanup failures are reported as warnings and retried.
.B --offline
requires cached authenticated metadata and artifacts.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/packslip/pins.d/*.toml
contains administrator trust constraints.
User state is under XDG_STATE_HOME/packslip, defaulting to ~/.local/state/packslip.
Root state is /var/lib/packslip and ignores HOME and user configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://packslip.dev/docs/bootstrap/
https://packslip.dev/docs/compatibility/
